<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chamadevi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">7th century (traditional)</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Camadevi, Jamadevi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chamadevi was the legendary first ruler of Hariphunchai, the Mon kingdom centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lamphun">Lamphun</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>. Northern Thai chronicles describe her as a princess of Lavo (Lopburi) invited by hermit founders to rule the new city, traditionally in the 7th century, bringing Buddhist monks and craftsmen with her. She is still venerated in Lamphun, though her historicity cannot be confirmed.</p></div>
